# TEMPLATE-INPUT PLACEHOLDER for the per-slot advertise address (ADR-0039 §7).
#
# The MH template (deployment.yaml) needs a resolvable configMapKeyRef for
# MH_WEBTRANSPORT_ADVERTISE_ADDRESS (dt-guard env-config resolves every ref
# against a generator in this base). This generator is that target and nothing
# else: infra/kind/scripts/deploy.sh EXCLUDES it (label
# dark-tower.io/mh-template-input) from every apply, and infra/kind/scripts/mh.sh
# rewrites the ref to slot k's real ConfigMap (mh-slot-<k>-config, rendered by
# deploy.sh:render_env_overlay from the slot table). A pod that ever ran from an
# unrewritten template would therefore fail closed (CreateContainerConfigError:
# no such ConfigMap) rather than advertise this value. The `.invalid` TLD
# (RFC 2606) makes the value undialable even if that guarantee were broken.
MH_WEBTRANSPORT_ADVERTISE_ADDRESS=https://mh-slot-unassigned.invalid:1
